From 5ee2c2d14470b6579b436ab730c70f9c9cd79640 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rayuga <adityapatkar81@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:20:42 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: acpi: Add ELAN1200 to i2c_acpi_force_100khz_device_ids

The ELAN1200 touchpad (HID 04F3:3104) on the ASUS VivoBook X571GD
becomes sluggish and occasionally jumps when the I2C bus runs at
400 kHz. The problem only appears with the AC charger connected.

The laptop DSDT describes the touchpad bus at 0x00061A80 (400 kHz).
Forcing the bus to 100 kHz removes the problem. The same workaround is
already applied to the ELAN06FA, ELAN0678, and ELAN1300 touchpads.

The DSDT override that forces 100 kHz was verified on an ASUS VivoBook
X571GD (BIOS X571GD.313) running a 6.18.y kernel. This patch provides
the equivalent kernel-level fix for unmodified firmware.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/bfd74cd1fbc026f04446e67d6915c7e199c2bffd
Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/9998e388be9930c106eb5904c23ecf2162407527
Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/9e9762e578db7556bea644bb5a8a2435f63544d1
Signed-off-by: Rayuga <adityapatkar81@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c
index 8f3bdd5..9fca13c 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-acpi.c
@@ -374,6 +374,7 @@ static const struct acpi_device_id i2c_acpi_force_100khz_device_ids[] = {
 	{ "DLL0945", 0 },
 	{ "ELAN0678", 0 },
 	{ "ELAN06FA", 0 },
+	{ "ELAN1200", 0 },
 	{ "ELAN1300", 0 },
 	{}
 };
-- 
